[center][img]{{title_card.png}}[/img]
[size=4][i]"Fireflies are pure light on dark. You can't paint them. I keep trying." - Sable[/i][/size]

[size=3]Pick up a brush. [b]Pelican Palette[/b] adds painting to Stardew Valley: a minigame as hands-on as fishing, a new skill, an art supply shop in Cindersap Forest, and Sable, the restorer who runs it.[/size]

[size=3]Set an easel down anywhere (in your farmhouse, by the river, on the summit) and paint what you see: a parsnip, a basket of fruit, a friend who'll sit for you, the view in front of you. Mix your colours against the light, copy the picture cell by cell, and sell, gift, frame or varnish what you make.[/size]

[img]{{update_1_3.png}}[/img]

[size=4][b]New in 1.3[/b][/size]
[quote]Margot Pell, a conservator from the city museum: a second romance, with six heart events, a cottage of her own and her own wedding
Twenty-one damaged old paintings to find, in five sets, in the ground, the sea, the mines, the desert and the volcano
Painting Mastery past level 10: pass Margot's test and restore old paintings yourself
The museum's collection, with rewards for every set, and a new Painting Wing to hang it in
Sixteen frame styles, from pine to Qi's, each with a bonus for the easels in its room, and a Framer's Bench to swap them
Paint your pet, your horse and your farm animals
Easels at Spirit's Eve and the Moonlight Jellies, and Sable's Winter Star gift
Five painting special orders, one of them Qi's
A last portfolio page, a gold-leaf frame, and a scene on the Summit
Julian buys a painting a season, and has a winter coat
Zoom in with the mouse wheel, and Relaxed keeps the whole picture (Simple pictures, if you'd rather)[/quote]

[img]{{header_features.png}}[/img]

[size=4][b]Painting[/b][/size]
[quote]Mix colours on a fishing-style bar, then copy the reference cell by cell
Paint before the light runs out, and catch inspiration sparks for more
Still lifes of anything in your bag, portraits of friends, the view outdoors, monsters you've slain, your animals, or your own original
Small, medium and large canvases
Glazing on medium canvases and highlights on large ones: the minigame grows with you
Quality from normal to iridium, set by your accuracy and your skill
Paint on linen, perfectly, and make a [b]Masterpiece[/b]
Learn colours like recipes; spend paint from your Palette; grind your own in a Pigment Mill
Wooden, Enamel and Iridium Palettes: tubes go straight in, and a palette set down stores your paint
Five brushes, from hog bristle to iridium, that wear like fishing tackle
Zoom in with the mouse wheel on big canvases; the reference zooms with you[/quote]

[img]{{paint_glaze.png}}[/img]

[img]{{palette_menu.png}}[/img]

[size=4][b]The Painting Skill[/b][/size]
[quote]A new skill from level 1 to 10, with its own skills-page bar (via SpaceCore)
New tools as you level: broad brush, ruler, mirror, dropper
Bigger canvases, rarer pigments, higher quality
Six professions: Plein Air, Steady Hand, Visionary, Gallerist, Patron's Favorite, Prolific[/quote]

[img]{{header_selling_and_keeping.png}}[/img]
[quote]Sell to Pierre, to the art shop for more, or through the shipping bin
Consign up to three paintings at Sable's gallery: they sell in a few days for more again
A new subject sells for more; the same one painted over and over in a week, for less, until Monday
A painting record of every subject you've painted, in tabs, with milestone rewards
A portfolio book of pages to fill, and a plan chest, in the shop's back room
Villagers' commissions on the art shop's board, portraits, varnished and glazed work included
Everyone loves an iridium painting, and nobody dislikes one
Frame paintings to hang on your walls, in sixteen styles: each one hung helps the easels in its room
Varnish them in a Varnishing Cabinet, which cures them like wine in a cask[/quote]

[img]{{results_masterpiece.png}}[/img]

[img]{{header_the_art_shop.png}}[/img]
[quote]A cottage shop west of the path down from Marnie's, marked on the world map
A yard easel you can paint at, still lifes or the view
Canvases, pigments, paint, brushes, frames, palettes, varnish and more, with stock that grows with your skill
A commission board, a consignment gallery, and your painting record at the counter
And, for one special evening, a gallery opening[/quote]

[img]{{shop_exterior.png}}[/img]

[img]{{header_sable_portrait.png}}[/img]
[quote]Sable (they/them), a former museum restorer from Zuzu City
Hundreds of lines of dialogue, a full schedule, and every festival
Their own room under the shop, down a trapdoor (from 2 hearts, or with the Key to the Town)
Winter and island outfits
Heart events at 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 14 hearts
A stall at the Night Market, all three nights
Watch them paint at the yard easel on Friday mornings
Dateable and marriageable, married in their own wedding suit, with a spouse room and patio, and they still keep the shop
Married, they paint the farm for you now and then[/quote]

[img]{{event_gallery_1.png}}[/img]

[img]{{header_margot_portrait.png}}[/img]
[quote]Margot Pell (she/her), a conservator from the Zuzu City Museum of Art, who trained with Sable
She arrives the week after you find your first old painting, and works at the museum
Her own room off the Saloon, then a cottage by the river that Robin builds her
Heart events at 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 14 hearts, and her own wedding
Dateable and marriageable by anyone, with a conservation corner and a patio easel of her own
She and Julian don't agree about restoration. At all.[/quote]

[img]{{margot_museum.png}}[/img]

[img]{{header_old_paintings.png}}[/img]
[quote]Twenty-one damaged old paintings in five sets, each found its own way
Margot restores them for a fee; with Painting Mastery, you restore them yourself at the easel, working out what's missing from what's left
Restored, they're worth far more than your own work
Give them to the museum: frames, gallery furniture, a living painting, Margot's loupe and a Junimo for the sets you finish
A Painting Wing at the museum, with a place for every painting[/quote]

[img]{{restore_mill.png}}[/img]

[img]{{header_the_valley.png}}[/img]
[quote]Julian Vane, a city art critic with a history with Sable, visits the 22nd to the 24th of every season, with five heart events of his own
A painting contest at the Stardew Valley Fair, judged by Julian
Sable's stall at the Night Market, and easels at Spirit's Eve and the Moonlight Jellies
Painting special orders on the town board, and one of Qi's[/quote]

